now  there's a receiver who has only one 100  yard receiving game this year his name  is emmanuel sanders emmanuel sanders  traded to the san francisco 49ers mds  just one day after coach kyle shanahan  suggested there's not much urgency this  year to upgrade at the position i  interpreted that as you can't come off  as desperate if you're trying to be a  buyer at the trade deadline here we are  with a week to go and may be sparked by  the muhammad sanu trade from atlanta to  new england it's emanuel sanders a guy  we knew was on the trade market he goes  from denver to san francisco and it's  sanders plus a five  for  a third round pick and a fourth round  pick from san francisco  and  ultimately  the four and the five maybe not all that  far apart because denver stinks so it'll  be a high five the 49ers are good so  it'll be a low four  so it's really a straight up three  almost  for emmanuel sanders when the patriots  gave up a second round pick to get  mohamed sanu  and i look i'm not shocked by this  but my guess is the 49ers if they were  going to make a move they'd rather have  muhammad sunu because he knows the kyle  shanahan offense he was in the shanahan  offense in atlanta when shanahan was  there as offensive coordinator  yeah i would bet that maybe the 49ers  got a little desperate when the patriots  pulled the trigger and the falcons  agreed on that sinew trade and it  wouldn't be surprising to know  that you know a lot of the time when we  talk about trades we say oh why why did  that team give up that much they they  could have gotten them for less right  but you never know what other offers are  out there  and uh you know it wouldn't be  surprising if maybe the 49ers were  dragging their feet just a little bit  on this new trade and the falcons just  said  best offer we've gotten is a two we're  ready to do it let's take the two before  you know something happens that you know  the patriots acquire some other wide  receiver like emmanuel sanders and now  they're not offering us a two anymore um  so so i found that pretty interesting  and yet you know the 49ers and the  patriots  probably the two best teams in the  league right now anyway uh it's very  interesting that they're both making  moves to try to make themselves better  and we've still got another week to go  before this trade deadline won't be  surprising if we see more of the  contenders  try to get some good players off more of  the teams that aren't going anywhere  especially because we now know more  about the teams that aren't going  anywhere last weekend's games this  weekend's games you combine the two and  you really can get to a level of comfort  after eight weeks  as to who's going to stink and who could  benefit from  using their current assets guys who may  not be there for the turnaround next  year use them now to get draft picks  that will help you get better the  falcons obviously know they stink and  the broncos after thursday night's  putrid performance offensively against  the chiefs and defensively they weren't  much better the broncos can come to the  conclusion it's time for them to sell as  well and it'll be interesting to see who  else is available from that denver team  chris harris jr cornerback in the last  year of his contract that's going to be  the next guy to keep an eye on and i  still think von miller can be had the  question is what will it take i don't  buy it anytime anyone says so and so  won't be traded o.j howard buccaneers  tight end won't be traded well if  somebody makes them an offer they can't  refuse o.j howard will be traded if the  broncos get an offer they can't refuse  for von miller von miller will be traded  now you can say generally no but  the end result may be yes and that's  part of the game that you have to play  in order to get the best value same  reason kyle shanahan says we're not  having that same sense of urgency we've  had in the past to get a receiver at the  trade deadline you say that to pay less  you say that you're not going to trade  the guy to get more and look at the  activity we've already had we still have  a full week four o'clock eastern next  tuesday is when that window closes and  there could be a lot of activity  although who knows maybe all the trades  will be done by then and there'll be  nothing left to do  yeah and and i really think when a team  puts out word like oh von miller  definitely won't be traded  i think what that actually means is  if you want von miller call us up with  an offer like two first round picks like  we've seen  jalen ramsey laramie tunsil it  that's really what they're communicating  it's not don't call us at all it's  be ready to offer us something really  good if you want us to talk about ivan  miller trade because uh  any player  can be traded for the right offer if  it's a good enough offer  any player can be traded now i i guess  there might be some franchise  quarterbacks who a team  just would say listen we're just not  interested but you know even a franchise  quarterback  if you got enough first-round picks in  in exchange for him maybe you'd think  about it so i i really believe that that  any player can be traded and certainly  von miller could be traded the real  question is is there a team that thinks  we are one good pass rusher away from  winning the super bowl if so  that team might call up with one of  those two first round picks and more  type of offers and von miller could move  yeah last week in the aftermath of the  jalen ramsay trade he harvested two  first-round picks and a fourth-round  pick for the jaguars we had some  conversations about guys you wouldn't  trade for two ones and a four and there  really aren't many guys that you would  say no way in hell to two ones and a  four the question is how many guys truly  are untouchable and  if a team is willing to put enough on  the table and those draft picks are  viewed as as so valuable for what they  mean a first round pick is five years at  a very relatively low rate in comparison  to free agent market value that it's  hard to say no when that opportunity  arises and we'll see if somebody at the  top end of the nfl's hierarchy right now  decides they want to make a run at a guy  like von miller or oj howard or other  guys that we've been told aren't  tradeable and aj green is the guy to  watch now at the receiver position  because he was the original receiver  that we were watching saying well surely  the patriots will make a play for him  and maybe the packers now will make a  play for him but if mohammed sunu is  worth a second round pick now i don't  know how healthy aj green is but i think  if sunu is worth a two a healthy aj  greens worth at least a first round pick  and maybe the patriots tried to get aj  green for a first round pick but bengals  looked at and said well it's a low first  round pick so we're not interested  yeah and the aj green situation is a  little different because he's in his  last year of his contract sunu has one  more year so  teams if you're gonna trade for aj green  i think you're either saying to yourself  we already know we're gonna franchise  him or you've talked to him and you've  gotten  if not a new deal worked out you at  least you and him and his agent at least  have a pretty good understanding of what  it'll take to get a deal done but yeah i  would agree i mean aj green is once he  gets healthy he's clearly a better wide  receiver than muhammad sunu better than  emmanuel sanders so it's going to take  something pretty good to get him but  again  the bengals of course if someone offers  them a first round pick for aj green i  think they have to do it  i think part of the problem here is it's  hard to get to the point where you're  comfortable trading for aj green and  signing aj green because he hasn't  played this year he had that injury  early in training camp no one's seen him  on a field i think recently both the  bengals and green have been going easy  on putting him back on the field because  the bengals want to be able to get trade  value green wants to leave or at least  wants to wait until he sees where he's  going to be a lot of moving parts to  make it work and you really have to take  a leap of faith if you're a new team  signing aj green to a long-term deal  because there's a chance he's not going  to be the guy that he was you may be  getting someone who is damaged good so i  think that makes it more difficult as  well so that's where the trade market  currently stands again another week to  go maybe a lot more activity as the  teams that are at the top try to go all  in and the teams at the bottom realize  that it's time to fold the tents and  live to fight another day with more  draft picks as opposed to veteran  players who won't be there when and if  things turn around  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

